  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which one amongst the following are good oxidising agents?</p><p>(a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sm</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>(b)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>(c)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>(d)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Tb</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "C only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "D only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A and B only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "C and D only",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The common oxidation state of lanthanide&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. The lanthanide ions having&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;oxidation state undergo oxidation readily, hence they act as reducing agents.&nbsp;The lanthanide ions having&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>oxidation state undergo reduction&nbsp;readily, hence they act as oxidising&nbsp;agents.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Tb</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math> act as oxidising agent</p>"
  }
}